# Python environment

This project runs exclusively inside the conda environment `general_env_1`
(Python 3.10.6). Never use the system Python, and never `pip install` globally.

Run every Python, pip, test, or console-script command through that env.
Use `--no-capture-output` for anything that prints Unicode (IPA, Rich tables);
otherwise conda re-encodes output as cp1252 on Windows and crashes/hangs.

```bash
conda run --no-capture-output -n general_env_1 nautical stats
conda run --no-capture-output -n general_env_1 pytest
conda run -n general_env_1 pip install -e .
conda run -n general_env_1 python ...
```

Or activate it first for an interactive shell:

```bash
conda activate general_env_1
```

Do not introduce `.venv`/`virtualenv` setups or invoke a bare `python` / `pip`
that could resolve to system Python.
